# Code owners for agent-harness.
#
# Single-maintainer repo today, so every line resolves to the same person. That
# is deliberate rather than redundant: the paths below are the ones where a
# review is load-bearing regardless of who is on the other side of it, and
# listing them now means the policy already exists when a second maintainer
# arrives instead of being retrofitted after the first bad merge.
#
# Order matters — the LAST matching pattern wins.

# Default owner for everything.
*                       @jtmurphysr

# ---------------------------------------------------------------------------
# Executable configuration. These run on an engineer's machine with that
# engineer's full privileges — no sandbox, no isolation. Hook config is code
# that ships in the repo, and it gets reviewed like build tooling.
# ---------------------------------------------------------------------------
/.claude/               @jtmurphysr
/.github/workflows/     @jtmurphysr
/.pre-commit-hooks.yaml @jtmurphysr

# ---------------------------------------------------------------------------
# Structural invariants. scripts/validate_harness.py enforces the module
# boundaries declared in AGENTS.md; changing either one changes what "done"
# means for every agent operating in this repo.
# ---------------------------------------------------------------------------
/AGENTS.md              @jtmurphysr
/scripts/validate_harness.py  @jtmurphysr
